{D.27 = 27-44}
141=27.	@wDN{An} raised his far-reaching gaze to the good shepherd. 
145=28.	He spoke to @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, his beloved son, with kindly words: @q[An,Ur-Ninurta]{“May there be shame at your awe-inspiring splendour, while you (?) ride as if on a great storm. 
149=29.	May you have no rival in your youthful power. 
153=30.	May the Land remain (?) under your rule. 
157=31.	May you make your name supreme in the foreign lands, and may they speak good of you. 
161=32.	May the land that is of its own will unbending to you, submit to you. 
165=33.	@wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, to whom I have given great power: you should trust in my name. 
169=34.	May your words clamp down upon the wicked like a great neck-stock. 
173=35.	May the rebel land approach at your command, and do reverence to you. 
177=36.	In your lordliness may you hold your head high. 
181=37.	May you be good to the people. 
185=38.	May you be the man of justice, and may it come to your aid. 
189=39.	You have justice that comes from the heart; you are one of @wDN{Utu's} retainers. 
193=40.	May @wDN{Inana}, who is assuredly your beloved, provide you with long life. 
197=41.	May the good protective deities of the @fsux{en} priesthood and of kingship stand faithfully at your side. 
201=42.	My @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, named with the name of @wGN{Sumer}! 
205=43.	Go with your head high to the shrine of @wSN{Nibru}, to @wTN{Dur-an-ki}. 
209=44.	Brick-built @wTN{E-kur} accepts your offerings: @q{“May the awe-inspiring shepherd stand in attendance with his great food offerings for the house.”}”} 

